Interpretation:
  latency=0us  is the ORIGINAL backtest. Includes bar closing AT entry_us.
  latency=1us  excludes that bar (paranoia check).
  latency=50-500ms is realistic WebSocket forwarding lag.
  latency=60s   uses ONLY bars that closed >=60s ago (most conservative).

If PPT halves going from 0us -> 100ms, the original alpha is mostly lookahead.
If PPT stable going from 0us -> 500ms, the alpha is real.
